    exists_tableFindTM at Γ : Type (option (b)); backlog UNIV-1 for option (a)
    
    The record-table continuation escalated that exists_tableFindTM, stated for
    Γ : Type*, cannot use its mandated loop: counterLoopTMVia and phaseHostTM take
    their alphabet in Type. The user chose to restate the row at Γ : Type, since
    every consumer's alphabet (RecSym Q T) lies in Type. One statement changes,
    flagged in its docstring; RecordTable elaborates with 0 errors. The option of
    generalizing the two hosts is recorded as backlog UNIV-1 (optional, 12.2c).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

